AI Powered Onboarding Agent​

Problem ststment:

The current API onboarding process, while automated, still requires manual input,
structured knowledge, and adherence to standards from developers. Users need to
understand Apigee requirements, metadata standards, and repository structures, which
can slow onboarding and introduce inconsistencies. There is a gap between developer
intent and platform implementation, leading to rework, validation failures, and longer
onboarding cycles.​

Prposed solution:

Introduce an AI-powered onboarding assistant (agent) integrated into the UI (e.g.,
Backstage or portal). Instead of filling static forms, users interact conversationally or via
guided prompts.​

​

The agent:​

Collects API requirements (name, endpoint, purpose, security, etc.)​

Interprets or generates OAS (if not provided)​

Automatically structures metadata​

​

The agent then:​

Creates GitLab branches/files via API​

Triggers pipelines​

Monitors progress and provides feedback to users​

Optionally, it can suggest improvements (naming, policies, security standards).​

How AI helps:

Reduces cognitive load: Developers don’t need deep knowledge of Apigee or internal standards​

Automates interpretation: Converts natural language → structured API definitions (OAS, metadata)​

Improves quality: Built-in validation, suggestions, and policy recommendations​

Closes feedback loop: Agent can explain pipeline failures and suggest fixes​

Leverages GitLab Duo:​

Code/OAS generation​

Pipeline insights​

Inline suggestions and automation

Business Value​

​

Faster API onboarding → reduced time-to-market​

Improved developer experience → higher adoption across teams​

Reduced rework → cost and effort savings​

​

​

Technology Value​

​

Standardised API definitions and policies​

Reduced validation errors and pipeline failures​

Scalable onboarding model across multiple teams​

Better integration with existing GitLab + CI/CD ecosystem​
